After many, many years of playing Nethack (and before that Moria and Larn) I
finally managed to win a game.

I wasn't even playing seriously. I just wanted to kill an hour so started
playing random characters. An archaeologist died quickly because he wasn't
being careful enough. A caveman died when that wand of create monster created
more orcs than he bargained for. Up next was a Valkyrie (really YAFAP ought to
be YAVAP) who wandered around on level 1, and in a corner there found "a
war hammer named Mjollnir". That seemed pretty interesting, and when lightning
struck my first newt it seemed that this might not be an ordinary game. BTW,
this game was played on nethack.alt.org, but I didn't find a single bones file
all game.

Found the mines early but they were dark so I continued on to 2 general
stores, the oracle and then sokoban. The first general store gave an oilskin
cloak which I later lost to a poly trap somewhere. As always I messed up the
last level of sokoban. I still hadn't found any light but I started the mines
anyway. Luckily there was only one dark level between the entrance and the
town where I was able to purchase some light. Somewhere around here I had been
whacking some bad stuff and my hammer was obviously worse for the wear, so I
went back to my longsword for the time being.

At the bottom of the mines I found a luckstone and a bunch of spellbooks. (I
didn't use any spells throughout the game, except to get confused.) Somewhere
I found some scrolls of enchant weapon and some booze, so now I'm wielding
Mjollnir again. Back to Sokoban and between my newly found pickaxe and scrolls
of earth I acquire an amulet of reflection.

Working my way down I found a magic whistle and a wand of
poly. I'd been trying to raise pets to the level of shopkeeper killer but they
just kept dying on me. I polyed my pet into a lich which seemed pretty cool.
Turns out he was slow and weak so I polyed him some more, killing him of
system shock. I quickly got another pet and polyed him into an iron golem,
named The Machine.

When saccing some more I got a number of useless swords including Dragonbane
which The Machine took to quite nicely. The Machine took out store owners and,
after buying some protection, the priest. The only priests in this game were
in mine town and the valley of the dead.

Down on level 12 was the quest portal, but I wasn't ready yet. On level 20 I
found a massive scroll store (6x9 of stuff iirc), and The Machine gladly
helped me pay for it all (2 hits per store). I still hadn't found a bag of
holding yet but it wasn't hurting me as bad as it usually does because I had a
number of stashes and returned to them frequently. I think I finally found a
BoH in level 20-something. Somewhere along the line I also found some water
walking boots which were very useful in making holy water.

Going down some more, I finally leveled up and found a wraith corpse so it was
time for the quest. Lord Surtur turned out to be a wimp, and after eating a
lot of giants my strength was up to 18/60 or so. Went down to Medusa's level
and the titan there summoned a mind flayer. Luckily my helm of brilliance
prevented any major disasters, but it was a little scary. The titan was also
nice enough to summon a cockatrice which solved the problem nicely. Medusa
died quickly. Then I went all the back up to level 4 or so where I dropped my
pickaxe. I think I found boots of levitation and a shield of reflection,
neither of which I used.

The castle was right below Medusa. After zapping all the eels I took the back
entrance, killing everything in sight. Got a bunch of scales but no
silver/gray. Wished for SDSM, speed boots, GoP, magic marker (for genocide h
and enchant armor), 2 scrolls of charging, and a silver saber to replace the
one that I found in mine town and had overenchanted. I polypiled for an extra
candle (Izchak only had 6), armor (shirt, helm of brilliance, another oilskin
cloak), and a few scrolls of enchant armor/weapon. Together with protection in
the valley of the dead that got my AC down to -36.

Going further down I killed Juiblex, Asmodeus, paid off Baalzebub, and killed
Orcus. +7 Mjollnir with +7 silver saber really is unstoppable. Down on level
49 I found the vibrating square, and after reading some spoilers I realized I
must have missed Vlad's tower. A friendly RNG gave me sunsword which made it
much easier to map out the mazes, so for a while I was twoweaponing sunsword
and my pickaxe. Finally found Vlad's tower on level 39. Took the candelabrum
and wore the amulet of life saving (first I'd found).

Now I went all the way to level 1, digging straight paths. I also made a bunch
of holy water (30+) and put together my final ascension kit. Went down to
visit Rodney. He was on me as soon as I entered his little chamber,
teleporting to the other side of me. Used a WoD which worked great, except his
book fell in the water and I didn't have any way of getting it out. So I
returned to my stash on level 25 to grab some wands of cold. While doing that
Rodney visited me twice, and I decided smacking him is almost as effective as
a wand of death. Back in the tower I used one of the wands to get my book out
of the water.

Headed down to the marked vibrating square. Did the song and dance and went
down. Killed some priests and Rodney, got the amulet. Ran out of there and up.
I think I saw Rodney twice more, and the mysterious force pulled me back 4 or
5 levels total. At this point I panicked a little when I realized I only had 3
scrolls of gold detection. A little later I figured that the Orb of Fate would
probably work too. So I went up onto the planes, which were easy. Use the Orb
to find the portal, then go to it, avoiding any fights. Made it to astral with
300-some hitpoints, and all stats except In and Ch maxed out.

While on the plane of water I'd put on my oilskin cloak, and I forgot to swap
it out for my [CoMR when I left it. Didn't seem to have been that big a deal
though, although I suspect that left me open to some nasty stuff that I was
lucky to avoid.

I tried right first. It was Famine, who went down quickly. Fighting my way in
only to discover it was Loki's temple. Went back out, and tried the middle
door. Pestilence made me Ill a few times but my unicorn horn worked fine.
Fought my way in to discover it was Tyr's altar. Went back out, and shortly
after had a sad feeling about my guardian angel. (The Machine had gone wild
when I feel through a trap door in Gehennon.) The angel had been pretty
worthless anyway, killing all those nice insects that act as a buffer from the
other nastiest.

Took Death head on with no scars to show for it. Finally made it into my
temple, killed the mimic that was defiling it, took a deep breath, and...
